.TH KEYWAVE 1 "March 2026" "Keywave Manual" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
keywave \- mechanical keyboard and mouse sound daemon for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B keywave
[\fB\-c\fR \fIconfig_file\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR \fIvolume\fR]
[\fB\-k\fR \fIsoundpack_dir\fR]
[\fB\-m\fR \fIsound_file\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B keywave
is a lightweight, low-latency background daemon that reads global keyboard and mouse
input events from the Linux evdev subsystem and plays mechanical switch / click audio feedback.
It runs independently of the display server, supporting both Wayland and X11 seamlessly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIpath\fR"
Specify the path to a custom configuration file. If not provided,
.B keywave
searches for \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/keywave/keywave.conf\fR or \fI~/.config/keywave/keywave.conf\fR.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-volume " \fIfloat\fR"
Set the audio playback volume. Must be a non-negative floating-point number (e.g. \fB0.8\fR, \fB1.0\fR).
Overrides the value in the configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keyboard\-pack " \fIpath\fR"
Specify the directory of the keyboard soundpack. The directory must contain a valid \fBconfig.json\fR file.
Overrides the value in the configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mouse\-sound " \fIpath\fR"
Specify the audio file to play upon mouse click events.
Overrides the value in the configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command usage and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/keywave/keywave.conf
Default per-user configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/keywave/keywave.conf
Fallback configuration file path if \fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR is unset.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Specifies the base directory where user configuration files are stored.
.TP
.B HOME
Used as a fallback to locate \fI~/.config\fR if \fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR is not defined.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run with default configuration:
.RS
.B keywave
.RE
.PP
Run with custom volume and soundpack:
.RS
.B keywave \-v 0.6 \-k /usr/share/keywave/sounds/cherrymx\-blue
.RE
.PP
Use a specific configuration file:
.RS
.B keywave \-c ~/my_keywave.conf
.RE
